    "raw": "Given:\n- Calvin has had 8 haircuts.\n- He needs 2 more haircuts to reach his goal.\n\nThe total number of haircuts needed is 8 (already had) + 2 (needed) = 10 haircuts.\n\nTo find the percentage towards his goal:\n- Number of haircuts he has = 8\n- Total number of haircuts needed = 10\n\nPercentage towards the goal = (Number of haircuts he has / Total number of haircuts needed) * 100\n= (8 / 10) * 100\n= 0.8 * 100\n= 80%\n\nSo, Calvin is 80% towards his goal.\n\nFINAL: 80",
